# Unavailable test inputs and verification limits

The redistributable development test suite and its reference inputs are
included; private rich-corpus data, private captures and trial credentials are
not. Passing main-fixture grades does not complete the remaining mod-write
failures. This document separates export exclusions, unavailable inputs and
historical test results; it does not turn missing or failing coverage into a
pass.

## Included tests and source-origin exclusions

`npm test` runs the package smoke check and `npm run test:suite` runs the
included Vitest suite. The export also includes the reference harness and
synthetic-v1, synthetic-v2, synthetic-v2-mod-probes,
synthetic-v3-mod-probes-ruby33 and write-battery-v1 inputs. Each fixture
manifest states its actual expected-output coverage; v3's new Ruby 3.2.3
evidence is render-only. The MySQL overlay is a fresh stock Ruby 3.2.3
capture, not the superseded Windows Ruby 3.3.12 recording.

Four captures still lack positive evidence establishing the origin of their
input records. Those captures and their three actual runtime test readers are
excluded from the export; they remain in private development history. Unknown
origin is not proof of private origin. The 29 tests whose public-source basis
was established remain included; a comment-only mention of an excluded input
does not remove a test that never reads it.

These exclusions are unfinished evidence work, not successful comparisons.
Restore the affected checks only after exact captured bytes are bound to
redistributable source inputs, or fresh stock-Ruby captures from committed
reproducible seeds replace them and the tests pass. Development-only tooling
tests are also excluded where their required tool is not part of the package.
The export manifest lists the actual shipped files; shipping the suite is not
a claim that every test has passed from this export.

## Remaining write failures

The complete mod probe's latest recorded checkpoint passes its rendering
comparisons but still fails 278 persistence comparisons, 303 side-effect
comparisons and 275 other-table write comparisons. These are executed
failures, not missing-input skips. The owner continues the implementation
repair; no full mod-write compatibility or release-readiness claim follows
from a limited correction. Exact counts, source and fixture are in
[EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md). Keep them failing until a fresh complete result
shows the actual differences are fixed.

## Historical missing-input counts

An earlier development run recorded 253 test cases requiring private or
external inputs. Its skipped cases were not passes, and its per-case receipt
is not redistributed. The table preserves that run's breakdown; it is not a
current inventory of the exported suite.

| Skipped cases | Input absent from this package | Verification status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 249 corpus | A private deck with rich content, local copies of the database behind a privately served deck, and pages recorded earlier from that deck as it was publicly served (stored in several parts), all required by the original comparisons | Unverified; the small committed synthetic fixtures do not replace these inputs. |
| 2 harness | Private source snapshot and hosted measurement configuration for page-subresource and search-suggestion observations | Unverified; offline sibling checks are a separate scope. |
| 2 deploy | Explicit trial database URL and token for real session creation/resolution/revocation and the read-only trial-deck census | Unverified; production credentials are not substituted. |

The two trial-database cases are included in that historical 253 total. They are not two
additional passing or executed cases. Supplying their declared inputs is what
allows those checks to run; this package creates no trial resource.

Real-deck behaviour rests on named hosted comparisons, made during
development, of a Ruby Decko site used as the comparison reference with a
hosted deployment of the port on the Bunny (bunny.net) edge platform, against
the same selected records. Those are development observations: no record of
them ships with this package, and none is one of the results in
[EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md). They establish
their stated routes and settings only, not arbitrary corpus compatibility.
The required settings are in [DEPLOYMENT.md](DEPLOYMENT.md).

Two PGlite concurrency cases need independent database sessions, which the
embedded database does not offer. They are skipped as not applicable; they
are not passes and are not part of the 253 missing-input cases. A recovery
run on a Linux machine during development, limited to the Node and SQLite
interfaces the recovery tools use, is likewise a development observation
with no record in this package; it is not a full-suite result.

## Historical suite observations

### Linux full-suite gate, 3 November 2026

The retained run manifest names source commit
`fc5917bb942bf151bfbe992827f46793cc3c6d4a`. This is an old-source run,
not an outcome for the current combined source or exported package. Its
recorded case results are:

| Runner | Passed | Failed | Skipped | Cancelled | Files with failures |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Vitest | 12,072 | 75 | 194 | not recorded | 40 |
| node:test | 1,814 | 99 | 3 | 68 | 44 |

The failure-file counts identify files containing failed results; they are
not additional failed cases to add to the case totals. The Node runner
records Node v22.23.3. The retained receipt includes incomplete gem-source
copies and MySQL routing failures **and ordinary assertion differences**.
These results have not all been classified as environmental, and the failed
or cancelled cases are not passes. Repair and rechecking remain ongoing.
No fresh whole-suite success for the current candidate is inferred from
targeted tests or the passing synthetic-fixture grades.

The counts come from the retained runner summary and its original source
manifest, not a rerun or a model estimate. Test inputs were copied for the
run; no controlled cache state is recorded for these suite totals. Private
machine paths, operational logs and input details are not redistributed.

### Windows development run, 2 November 2026

A complete development run on 2 November 2026 on a Windows
workstation at an earlier source recorded 12,068 passing tests,
30 failed assertions and 149 pending tests under Vitest, plus 12 test files
that failed as a whole, and 1,996 passing and 5 failing tests under Node's
test runner. The project's reading of those 47 failures found none to be a
difference between the port and Ruby: 39 were tests that need the Linux
reference machine and could not reach it from that workstation, 3 were test
expectations older than a change to the default unsubscribe refusal, 4 came
from one defect in a staging build-freshness test, and 1 was a test file
whose tests were all skipped. That historical triage is not a statement that
the current implementation has no Ruby differences: the newer complete
mod-write probe above records actual mismatches. Later targeted Linux checks
and passing synthetic-fixture grades are not substituted for a complete
exported-suite result.
Separately, a test of the export tool failed 9 of its 12 cases, first on
Linux and then also on Windows, because the test's own stand-in module table
lacked a module the export tool had started to import. The corrected test
passed 12 of 12 on the Linux reference machine on 3 November 2026, and the
correction is in the source this package was exported from.

The package smoke check covers runtime assets and a synthetic render; its
`test:suite` command is a separate test run. Neither an export privacy check
nor a smoke pass establishes full behavior compatibility, private-deck
migration or hosted acceptance.
